Technical Manager I/II (holding the functional title of Clerk of Works/Building Services Inspector/Assistant Clerk of Works/Assistant Building Services Inspector)

Technical Manager I/II (holding the functional title of Clerk of Works/Building Services Inspector/Assistant Clerk of Works/Assistant Building Services Inspector) in the Project Division of the Estates Office (Ref.: 534705)

We are looking for Technical Manager I/II (holding the functional title of Clerk of Works/Building Services Inspector/Assistant Clerk of Works/Assistant Building Services Inspector) to join the Estates Office.

The appointee will participate in campus expansion projects.  He/she will be an all-rounded candidate who will undertake comprehensive project duties from inception to post-completion.  He/she will also be responsible for providing administrative and clerical support; exercising budget, programme planning and quality control; and coordinating with various parties including consultants, government authorities, internal user groups, and in-house bodies in relation to project execution.

A Bachelor’s degree or above in Building Services (Electrical and Mechanical), Architecture, Civil/Structural Engineering, or a building/interior design-related discipline;

At least 8 years’ relevant experience at a supervisory level in project planning, management, site supervision and customer relationship management;

Experience in defect management, including liaising directly with main contractors/sub-contractors;

Good communication skills with the ability to work effectively with internal user groups;

Capability to troubleshoot complaints, log defects and provide progress updates;

Proven ability to conduct regular site inspections to assess the quality of remedial works, ensuring compliance with established standards and university specifications;

A solid understanding of building construction, MEP (Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing) systems;

Technical proficiency combined with strong emotional intelligence, and the capability to handle staff and student complaints with patience and diplomacy; and

A valid Construction Industry Safety Training Certificate (Green Card) issued in accordance with Chapter 59 of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (i.e. by attending the relevant safety training courses which are recognized by the Commissioner for Labour) or equivalent.

Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for appointment as Technical Manager II.

The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary full-time contract basis.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.

The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.   Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until March 26, 2026 or until the post is f

Director of Educational Technology (at the rank of Senior Assistant Registrar/Assistant Registrar) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (Ref.: 534687)

We are seeking a strategic and dynamic leader to assume the role of Director of Educational Technology, to foster AI initiatives in teaching and learning across the university community.

The appointee will oversee the strategic planning, implementation, and assessment of AI initiatives aimed at advancing teaching and learning at HKU.  The role entails promoting innovative AI-driven solutions, integrating advanced technologies into teaching and learning activities, and cultivating a culture of educational transformation across the university.

Develop and implement the AI strategy to support innovative teaching and learning initiatives;

Lead the integration of AI tools and platforms into curriculum delivery, assessment, and student support;

Collaborate with faculty and staff to promote AI adoption and provide training on AI technologies;

Engage with internal and external stakeholders to advance AI-driven educational solutions;

Ensure ethical use of AI, data privacy, and responsible AI practices within the university;

Monitor and evaluate the impact of AI initiatives on teaching and learning;

Promote awareness of AI innovations through internal and external communication channels.

A University degree, preferably a higher degree, in AI, Computer Science, Education Technology, Data Science, or related field;

10-15 years of experience in digital transformation at higher education or complex organizations, with at least 5 years’ experience at managerial role.  Experience in a university setting is an advantage but not mandatory;

Proven leadership in AI application, development, and implementation within complex organizations;

Experience integrating AI into teaching and learning environments is highly desirable;

Strong knowledge of AI, machine learning, natural language processing, and data analytics;

Familiarity with educational technologies and digital learning platforms;

Demonstrated ability to lead multidisciplinary teams and develop strategic plans;

Excellent communication, stakeholder engagement, and collaboration skills;

Commitment to ethical AI, data privacy, and responsible technology use;

Candidates with less experience may be considered for appointment as Assistant Registrar.

Senior Technical Manager (holding the functional title of Senior Sports Development Manager)

Senior Technical Manager (holding the functional title of Senior Sports Development Manager) in the Centre for Sports and Exercise (Ref.: 534457)

The University of Hong Kong (HKU) is looking for an inspiring, strategic, and dynamic leader to champion the development of sport and physical activity across the University community in the Centre for Sports and Exercise (CSE).

The CSE is dedicated to fostering a vibrant culture of sports, wellness, and community at HKU. We manage world-class facilities like the Stanley Ho Sports Centre and deliver comprehensive programmes that serve students, staff, alumni, and the wider community, supporting the University's commitment to holistic education and excellence.

Reporting to the CSE Director, this senior role carries the responsibility for setting the long-term vision and strategic direction for all sports development, recreational programming, and athlete support at HKU.  The appointee will lead the effort to elevate our sporting culture, enhance competitive excellence, and ensure our programmes are inclusive, innovative, and integrated into the student experience.  The appointee will also provide strategic leadership to the sports development team, moving beyond programme management to shape policy and legacy.

•   Formulate and lead the CSE’s overarching sports and recreation strategy, setting long-term goals for participation, performance, and community engagement;

•   Provide strategic leadership and direction to the sports development team, fostering a high-performance culture that supports both elite athletes and broad-based participation;

•   Develop and implement a visionary framework for University Sports Teams, athlete scholarship schemes, and high-performance support, ensuring alignment with top-tier university sports standards;

•   Drive innovation in sports programme design, leveraging technology (e.g., AI, data analytics) and evidence-based practice to enhance coaching, training, and participant outcomes;

•   Forge and manage high-level strategic partnerships with key external bodies such as The University Sports Federation of Hong Kong, China, national sports associations, and community organizations;

•   Oversee major sports event strategy and policy, positioning HKU as a premier host for significant competitions and inclusive campus sporting events;

•   Champion sports as a key pillar of student life and alumni connection, working collaboratively across the University to embed a vibrant, lifelong sports culture;

•   Contribute to resource development and fundraising initiatives specifically for sports programmes and facilities.

•   A good postgraduate degree, preferably at the Master's level or above, in Sports Management, Exercise Science, Education, or a related field;

•   Not less than 10 years’ proven experience in strategic sports development and leadership, with a significant po

We are seeking a high-calibre professional with exceptional skills and potential to join the President’s Office as Assistant Registrar, supporting the portfolio of Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Teaching and Learning) (“VP/PVC (T&L)”).

The appointee will serve as an administrative lead overseeing all aspects of administration for the central units under the VP/PVC (T&L)’s portfolio, such as Co-operative Education Office, Common Core Office, Cultural Management Office, HKU Horizons Office, and Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre. Working closely with the VP/PVC (T&L) and other administrative units of the University, he/she will play a key role in ensuring administrative effectiveness, coordination and operational support across the relevant units. Key responsibilities include but are not limited to:

Supporting the development, implementation and review of University‑wide strategies, policies and initiatives related to teaching and learning;

Facilitating coordination across academic and administrative units within the University and with external bodies to promote innovative, future‑ready and student‑centred teaching and learning practices;

Providing leadership and oversight for a full spectrum of administrative operations of the central units under the Vice-President (Teaching and Learning)’s portfolio;

Providing high-level secretariat support for committees and working groups related to teaching and learning, including preparation of discussion papers, reports and submissions;

Performing other duties as assigned in support of the VP/PVC (T&L)’s portfolio and in the President’s Office.

At least 10 years of relevant administrative and management experience in sizable organizations, with sound understanding of teaching and learning in a tertiary education environment;

Demonstrated leadership, organizational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and exercise sound judgement;

Excellent communication skills in written and spoken English and Chinese, with the ability to present ideas convincingly.

A strong sense of responsibility, professionalism and commitment to excellence; and

A high level of computer and AI literacy, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment.

The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for two years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable.

The University only accepts online applications for this post. Applicants should apply at the University’s careers site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as

Legal Executive/ Legal Secretary/ Legal Clerk (at the rank of Clerk I/II)

Legal Executive/ Legal Secretary/Legal Clerk (at the rank of Clerk I/II) in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 534575)

The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under the University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and is dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies. HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who pursue career advancement and success.

Assist in preparing and formatting legal documents, reports and correspondence;

Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including Cantonese and Putonghua);

Proficiency in PC applications such as MS Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint and Outlook;

Highly self-motivated, hardworking, and able to work independently under minimal supervision.

The appointment will be made on a two-year fixed-term full-time contract, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits.

The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University's career site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from March 19, 2026 and continue until April 3, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University thanks applicants for their interest, but advises that only shortlisted applicants will be notified of the application result.

