Manager, Marketing for MBA Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer)

Manager, Marketing for MBA Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref: 534584) (to commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance)

Applicants should possess a bachelor’s degree, with at least 5 years’ work experience, preferably in the field of marketing or in the tertiary education sector.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English; good organisational, interpersonal and communication skills; and IT proficiency.  They should also be good team players and outcome-driven professionals with the ability to plan, implement, and execute marketing strategies for the MBA programmes.  In addition, they should have great self-motivation and attention to details; a sense of urgency; an outgoing personality; and the ability to work independently.

The appointee will support the Marketing and Admissions of MBA programmes with diversified duties, such as marketing content development for social media channels, digital campaign execution, advertising and marketing collateral preparation, as well as website updates and database management.  The appointee will be responsible for developing, implementing, and managing digital marketing strategies that enhance brand awareness, increase web and social media traffic, and drive conversions.

• developing and executing comprehensive digital marketing strategies across various channels, including SEO, PPC, social media (English and Chinese), email marketing, and content marketing;

•analysing and reporting on performance metrics to assess the effectiveness of campaigns and make data-driven decisions;

• managing and optimising the company website and ensure it is user-friendly and optimised for search engines;

• creating engaging content that aligns with target audience needs and business objectives;

• overseeing the planning and execution of digital advertising campaigns, including budget management and performance tracking;

• building and maintaining relationships with external vendors and partners, including agencies and media outlets; and

The appointee will work at the Faculty’s Cyberport campus and may be required to work outside normal office hours, during weekends and traveling outside Hong Kong.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.

A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.

The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence

We are looking for an Executive Assistant to join our Faculty Office to provide support to the administration of our postgraduate programmes and research activities.

The appointee will be responsible for a mix of administrative and coordination work, including:

Supporting postgraduate programmes – handling admissions and examinations;

Assisting with research administration – helping with grant applications and related processes;

Managing enquiries and operations – liaising with students, Faculty members, and external parties while keeping records organized; and

Fresh graduates are also welcome to apply; on-the-job training will be provided;

A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua);

Strong organizational skills, good IT proficiency, attention to detail, ability to multitask, and self-motivation;

A good team player with a strong sense of responsibility and willingness to learn.

The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits.  The University is dedicated to supporting the professional development of its staff members and career development programmes and workshops are provided to enhance job-specific knowledge and skills.

The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until March 23, 2026, or until the position is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a written test and interview.

