Assistant Manager (Marketing and Events) (at the rank of Executive Officer)

Department: Communications and Public Affairs Office, Registry (60330)

Assistant Manager (Marketing and Events) (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Communications and Public Affairs Office of the Registry (Ref.: 534577)

The Communications and Public Affairs Office (CPAO) of the Registry of the University of Hong Kong (HKU) enhances HKU's reputation through branding, events, digital communications, media relations, and more. The office is also responsible for University events and ceremonies, publications, both external and internal communications, crisis management and community engagement. We are looking for talented candidates to join the team.

Support the Assistant Director and Senior Manager in the effective development and implementation of marketing and community engagement activities;

Plan, co-ordinate and manage various kinds of ceremonial and public activities to promote the University’s image;

Develop and execute the publicity plans for various activities of the University;

Engage both internal and external parties in developing marketing materials, including brochures, booklets, invitations, events video highlights, onsite decoration etc.;

Plan and coordinate project schedules, manage procurement processes to commission third-party service providers for various University initiatives;

Support office and University activities, which may require occasional work outside regular office hours.

We are seeking a motivated individual who possesses the following skills and experience:

At least five years’ experience in events management, marketing and hospitality; experience in supervising junior staff is an advantage;

Proficiency in both written and spoken English, Chinese and Putonghua;

Strong computer skills, including proficiency in MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint;

Proficient in web technologies, knowledge about social media platform trends, and skilled in data analytics for marketing; knowledge of multimedia, graphic design, and video-editing tools is a plus;

Excellent communication and presentation skills for collaborating with internal faculties and vendors;

Ability to manage fast-paced projects, multitask, and meet deadlines through effective prioritisation and planning;

Detail-oriented, self-motivated, and able to work independently under pressure;

Strong values of integrity, teamwork, and commitment to providing excellent service;

Experience in working in the higher education and service sectors is a bonus; and

Data Analyst (at the rank of Technical Officer / Research Assistant I/II)

Data Analyst (at the rank of Technical Officer/Research Assistant I/II) in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 534504)

The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies.  HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who are devoted to a career in the clinical trial profession.

Clinical data management and analysis is a core process in any clinical research project, and is subject to stringent international standards, guidelines and regulations such as CDISC (SDTM/ADaM).  HKU-CTC’s Data Management and Medical Statistics Unit is seeking talents who are interested/experienced in practising the data science/statistics profession in clinical research.

Collaborate with a team of biostatisticians and data management specialists on data standards, statistical programming and database development;

Support study setup for various data acquisition systems, including electronic Case Report Form (eCRF) design and EDC study configuration;

Develop programming specifications, deliverables and related documentations, including CDISC SDTM and ADaM datasets/analysis files, and tables, listings, and figures (TLFs) for statistical analysis and/or regulatory submission;

Develop data validation, review and reporting tools to support ongoing data management;

Perform quality assurance and quality control for all data management and programing activities; and

Bachelor’s degree or above in Data Science, Statistics, Biostatistics, Information Technology or related disciplines;

Solid knowledge in SAS and R programming for data manipulation, analysis and reporting;

Relevant experience in data management and statistical/database programming are added advantages;

Good interpersonal, problem-solving and project management skills;

Detail-minded, self-motivated and able to work as a good team player with positive service attitude; and

Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (proficiency in Putonghua is an advantage).

The appointment will be made on a two-year fixed-term full-time contract, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits.

