Manager, Communications and Public Relations (at the rank of Executive Officer)

Manager, Communications and Public Relations (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 534530) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance)

Applicants should possess a good bachelor’s degree, with about 6 to 8 years of full-time work experience in event management, communications, public relations, marketing, or a related field.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken Chinese (including Putonghua) and English; outstanding organisational, communication, project management, and problem-solving skills; a high level of computer literacy; and the ability to multitask under pressure, work well both independently and in a team, as well as work with people from a broad range of backgrounds internally and externally.   A can-do attitude and strong prioritisation skills are essential.  Experience in managing social media platforms would be an advantage. They should also be a keen learner with a curious mindset, willing to take that extra step to explore new ideas and contribute proactively.

The appointee will support the Faculty’s Communications and Public Relations Team in planning, developing, and implementing corporate communications strategies for brand promotion.  Responsibilities of the appointee include but not limited to the followings:

• planning and implementing a variety of high-standard events, including summits, ceremonies, conferences, seminars, workshops, partnership development events, and other campaigns;

• providing a full range of support on event management, including organisation, programme development, budgeting, scheduling, communication, logistics, coordination with various teams, and handling inquiries;

• sourcing and negotiating with vendors, suppliers, and venues to secure necessary services and resources for events;

• overseeing on-site event operations, including setup, coordination of staff and other project members, and troubleshooting any issues that may arise;

• generating and managing both online and offline communication materials for campaigns, such as advertisements, speeches, eDMs, invitations, presentations, booklets, videos, press releases, and multimedia posts across various channels to effectively engage target audiences.

• conducting post-event evaluations and analysis to assess against goals and KPIs, and to consolidate insights, areas for improvement, and best practices;

• undertaking any other duties assigned by the Faculty Office.

Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.

A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefi

Hall Executive (at the rank of Clerk II) in Jockey Club Student Village III

We are currently seeking a Hall Executive to join Jockey Club Student Village III (ref: 534475) in providing administrative support and ensuring smooth operations in our student residence.

Assist with the administration and operations of a cluster of residences, and be responsible for general office administration;

Maintain inventory of office supplies, handle procurement, and ensure stock availability;

Record income and expenses, process invoices and payments, and assist with various financial tasks;

Offer support to student residents by addressing their inquiries and concerns; and

Coordinate residents’ move-ins, move-outs and room relocations.

The appointee may be deployed to various clusters of student residences based on operational needs, as determined by the Dean of Student Affairs.

Preferably a recognized University degree, OR at least completed Form 5 or above, with 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics; OR a min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE, including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics;

